# M4.24 final regression count diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-28

## Failure

The final local validation redirected non-verbose `unittest` output and then
attempted to count lines beginning with `test_`. Non-verbose output contains a
dot progress line instead, so `grep` returned one and `set -e` stopped the
remaining validation commands.

## Impact

The regression itself completed successfully: `Ran 166 tests` and `OK` are
present in the captured log. Compilation, JSON, shell and static checks in that
combined command did not run after the counter failure. No repository, GitHub
or server state changed.

## Correction and rollback

The final validation is rerun without parsing individual test lines. Its native
`Ran 166 tests` result is used directly, followed by every remaining check as
separate fail-closed commands. This diagnosis is documentation-only; rollback
is a normal Git revert with the rest of the unactivated M4.24 branch.
